{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/NavajoKit\/documentation\/NavajoKit\/NavajoTagger-Model","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NavajoTagger.mlmoodel"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is Apple’s CoreML flavor of the part-of-speech tagger model, called the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/createml\/creating-a-word-tagger-model"},{"type":"text","text":" model. This model uses the conditional random field (CRF) algorithm for applying the appropriate parts-of-speech to recognize or inferred words. Alternate transfer-learning algorithems using BERT and ELMo are not possible for Navajo."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Statistics","anchor":"Statistics","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"41,755 training tokens","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"11,587 training records","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"23 parts-of-speech","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"90.4% model accuracy"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Usage","anchor":"Usage","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model is integrated into the classes of the NavajoKit framework so that no additional work is needed."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: > As a stand-alone, it will work on iOS 12.0+, macOS 10.14+ (Mojave), tvOS 12.0+, watchOS 5.0+, visionOS 1.0+."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Format-Conversion","text":"Format Conversion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you would like to convert it to another format to use outside the Apple ecosystem, here are a few methods that ","type":"text"},{